{"actor":"literature","data":{"citation":{"first_author":"Yohanes Dimas Pratama","identifier":"doi:10.30871/jaic.v9i3.9353","title":"Comparison of Data Normalization Techniques on KNN Classification Performance for Pima Indians Diabetes Dataset","year":2025},"claim":"Min-Max Scaling significantly improves KNN classification performance in terms of accuracy and ROC AUC.","concepts":["feature scaling","standardization","nearest neighbor","accuracy"],"id":"E1","quote":"The results show that Min-Max Scaling provides a significant improvement in all metrics, with the highest accuracy of 0.8117 and ROC AUC of 0.8050.","stance":"supports"},"hash":"88eb413dff7c105e79f68306b246f110a1362c1c9bc634c4eab341003b9f226b","kind":"artefact","prev":"17718003507ee6184b702c1756ba925d684a7f1f5984fcb948f15be56f7ceef5","seq":12,"stage":"evidence","ts":"2026-10-10T03:22:53.641+00:00"}
{"actor":"literature","data":{"citation":{"first_author":"P. V","identifier":"doi:10.1109/icfts62006.2025.11031668","title":"Optimizing Diabetic Retinopathy Screening with Machine Learning: A Data-Driven Approach","year":2025},"claim":"Feature scaling is part of the preprocessing pipeline in a KNN-based machine learning model for diabetic retinopathy screening.","concepts":["feature scaling","standardization","nearest neighbor","accuracy"],"id":"E2","quote":"Preprocessing involves resizing, normalization, fundus image data augmentation, and tabular data feature scaling.","stance":"supports"},"hash":"f6566df680f8bf0a9fe7aa20d9932f94a132cdcdb412126328344a448b43ebbf","kind":"artefact","prev":"88eb413dff7c105e79f68306b246f110a1362c1c9bc634c4eab341003b9f226b","seq":13,"stage":"evidence","ts":"2026-10-10T03:22:53.641+00:00"}
