{"actor":"hypothesis","data":{"dependent_variable":"classification accuracy","evidence_ids":["E1","E2"],"expected_direction":"increase","gap_ids":["G1"],"id":"H1","independent_variable":"scaling method (Z-score vs. Min-Max)","rationale":"This hypothesis directly addresses the gap in G1 by comparing different standardisation techniques (Z-score vs. Min-Max) on a non-uniform dataset, testing whether Z-score, which is more robust to outliers, performs better in accuracy. The evidence from E1 and E2 confirms that standardisation improves KNN performance, but does not compare techniques—this hypothesis fills that gap.","statement":"Z-score standardisation improves KNN classification accuracy more than Min-Max Scaling on tabular data with skewed feature distributions."},"hash":"fb1b9cde220c83cbaec8b9e1bd9e332d66cac42bf432446c81af603eb06d5901","kind":"artefact","prev":"ea0494147365af23eeec47c4c4d548092658b6b0286e4d210e4cf3bc9420f8db","seq":20,"stage":"hypotheses","ts":"2026-10-10T03:22:53.642+00:00"}
{"actor":"hypothesis","data":{"dependent_variable":"precision","evidence_ids":["E1","E2"],"expected_direction":"no_difference","gap_ids":["G2"],"id":"H2","independent_variable":"feature scaling (applied or not)","rationale":"This hypothesis addresses the gap in G2 by testing performance beyond accuracy and ROC AUC—specifically precision. It challenges the assumption that scaling uniformly improves performance, by testing whether scaling impacts recall or precision in the presence of outliers. The current evidence only reports accuracy and ROC AUC, so this test would explore underreported performance aspects.","statement":"Feature scaling has no significant effect on precision or recall in KNN classification for tabular data with high outlier presence."},"hash":"4052aef82752f54edc91150a9ba1c2f01b68aa04f55664818f8b519901136c5a","kind":"artefact","prev":"fb1b9cde220c83cbaec8b9e1bd9e332d66cac42bf432446c81af603eb06d5901","seq":21,"stage":"hypotheses","ts":"2026-10-10T03:22:53.642+00:00"}
